Package: ares-baseline
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Provides:
 nes-emulator,
Conflicts: ares-performance
Breaks: ares (<= 147+dfsg-1)
Replaces: ares (<= 147+dfsg-1)
Description: Accurate multi-system emulator (no n64 support)
 ares is an emulator for systems from Atari, Nintendo, Sega, Sony, NEC, SNK,
 Microsoft, Coleco, Bandai and Benesse. It is a descendent of higan and bsnes
 and focuses on accuracy and preservation. The SNES emulation is especially
 complete and polished.
 .
 Nintendo 64 support requires advanced SIMD instructions provided by x86-64-v2
 (amd64) and ARMv8+ (arm64) and is not included in this package. 

Package: ares-performance
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 x86-64-v2-support [amd64],
Provides:
 nes-emulator,
Conflicts: ares-baseline
Breaks: ares (<= 147+dfsg-1)
Replaces: ares (<= 147+dfsg-1)
Description: Accurate multi-system emulator (with n64 support)
 ares is an emulator for systems from Atari, Nintendo, Sega, Sony, NEC, SNK,
 Microsoft, Coleco, Bandai and Benesse. It is a descendent of higan and bsnes
 and focuses on accuracy and preservation. The SNES emulation is especially
 complete and polished.
 .
 This is the perfomance-orientated package built with x86-64-v2 or ARMv8+
 support.
